  "articleBody": "Roof flashing is your roof’s unsung hero, quietly diverting water away from vulnerable areas like chimneys, skylights, and vents. But when it starts to fail, it can quickly lead to leaks and significant damage. Knowing when to call in a professional for a flashing assessment can save you a lot of grief and expense. Ignoring these signs, especially with the intense weather in Texas, is a recipe for disaster.\n\nHere are some key indicators that it's time to get a pro to look at your roof flashing:\n\n*   **Visible Damage:** If you can see flashing that's cracked, corroded, loose, separated, or punctured, that's a clear red flag. These aren't just cosmetic issues; they're direct pathways for water to enter your home. Often, you can spot these problems from the ground with binoculars, or during a safe visual check of lower rooflines. Don't assume a little bend or rust isn't a big deal.\n\n*   **Water Stains Inside:** Any signs of water stains or discoloration on your attic ceiling, interior walls, or even around fireplace mantels are strong indicators of a leak, and flashing is a prime suspect. Water can travel, so a stain on your living room ceiling might originate from a flashing issue near the chimney or a vent a few feet away. A professional can trace the leak’s true source.\n\n*   **Deteriorated Sealant:** If the sealant around your flashing looks old, cracked, or is peeling away, it's losing its effectiveness. While caulk isn't a permanent fix for flashing, it often serves as a secondary seal. When it fails, it leaves the underlying flashing exposed to potential vulnerabilities. This is a common point of failure and an easy target for water intrusion, especially during heavy Texas rains.\n\n*   **After Severe Weather:** Texas frequently experiences hail, high winds, and heavy downpours. Even if you don't see immediate damage, severe weather can stress and compromise flashing. A professional assessment after a major storm can catch subtle issues before they develop into full-blown leaks. It’s a proactive step that can prevent much larger repair bills.\n\n*   **Aging Roof:** As your roof ages, so does its flashing. Materials can wear down, expand, and contract, leading to fatigue. If your roof is nearing the end of its lifespan, or even if it’s just several years old, a professional flashing assessment is a good part of a comprehensive maintenance plan to identify age-related vulnerabilities.\n\nWhen Professional Guidance Helps\nProfessional help becomes crucial when flashing is concealed, integrated with masonry or siding, associated with active or recurring leaks, or located on a steep or high roof. These situations require specialized knowledge and safety equipment to properly assess and address the issues.\n\nWhat to Do Next\nIf you've noticed any of these signs, don't delay. Contact Discounted Roofing Co. for a professional roof flashing condition assessment. We'll provide an honest evaluation and clear solutions to protect your home.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-03"
